{"availability":"available","full":"dcarrillo/whatismyip","name":"whatismyip","description":"Just another \"what is my IP address\" service, including DNS discovering, geolocation and headers information. Written in go with high performance in mind.","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":65,"forks":15,"created":"2021-11-10T19:04:58Z","updated":"2026-09-18T18:11:38Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ifconfig.es","topics":["geolocation","go","golang","whatismydns","whatismyip"],"demo":null,"color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.039Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.039Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.039Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.039Z","stars":65,"forks":15}],"technologies":["Go"],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:05.989Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Since version 3.2.0, an optional prometheus metrics endpoint is available. Since version 3.0.0, the geodb database is not mandatory; not adding the flags will disable the geo feature. Since version 2.3.0, the application includes an optional client DNS discovery feature.","Just another \"what is my IP address\" service, including geolocation, TCP open port checking, and headers information. Written in Go with high performance in mind, it uses gin which uses httprouter, a lightweight high-performance HTTP multiplexer.","Take a look at ifconfig.es, a live site using whatismyip with the DNS discovery feature enabled."],"features":["Experimental HTTP/3 support. HTTP/3 requires a TLS server running (-tls-bind), as HTTP/3 starts as a TLS connection that then gets upgraded to UDP. The UDP port is the same as the one used for the TLS server.","DNS discovery: A best-effort approach to discovering the DNS server that is resolving the client's requests.","Can run behind a proxy by trusting a custom header (usually X-Real-IP) to figure out the source IP address. It also supports a custom header to resolve the client port, if the proxy can only add a header for the IP (for…","Geolocation info including ASN. This feature is possible thanks to maxmind GeoLite2 databases. In order to use these databases, a license key is needed. Please visit Maxmind site for further instructions and get a free…","Checking TCP open ports."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dcarrillo/whatismyip/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"151959d5f0a01da82cc0cfa553391ce87b194967644d414760d8aa2d29f8445b","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:15:06.500Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:05.986Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-18T18:11:38Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Since version 3.2.0, an optional prometheus metrics endpoint is available. Since version 3.0.0, the geodb database is not mandatory; not adding the flags will disable the geo feature. Since version 2.3.0, the application includes an optional client DNS discovery feature.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dcarrillo/whatismyip/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"151959d5f0a01da82cc0cfa553391ce87b194967644d414760d8aa2d29f8445b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dcarrillo/whatismyip/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:05.987Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dcarrillo/whatismyip/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:05.988Z","hash":"151959d5f0a01da82cc0cfa553391ce87b194967644d414760d8aa2d29f8445b","originalBytes":9299,"storedBytes":9299,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["run","test","dns","server","http","port","string","tls","whatismyip","bash","client","tcp","docker","curl","default","discovery","geo","geoip2-asn","geoip2-city","using","version","address","custom","geoip2-city-test.mmdb","geolite2-asn-test.mmdb","header","information","metrics","path","request","set","template","tls-bind","build","databases","dns.example.com","dns.ifconfig.es","download","enables","file","headers","ifconfig.es","mandatory","proxy","resolver